{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception capabilities, separating motion commands from sensor outcomes. The specification encodes a conservative exploration policy: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are used only when obstacles are detected. Full_rotate is reserved for rare, persistent blockages. The supervisor avoids oscillations and overconstraining, always returning to exploration after recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion and perception to reflect open-loop actuation and asynchronous sensing.",
